{
  "_name": "s31_dual_carrier_gateway",
  "_desc": "Dual-CARRIER two-layer gateway (2026-07-26, Wave-4 #5). Copy of s09_two_layer_gateway with the two layers moved onto SEPARATE RF carriers: layer 4 @ 868.0 MHz, layer 5 @ 869.5 MHz. Proves the frequency-selective PHY: l4_* and l5_* nodes remain in DIRECT RF range in the topology matrix, yet cannot hear each other at all -- every cross-layer delivery must go through a gateway, which is deaf to the far layer for the whole of each window. Pre-#5 the carriers were ignored and the leaves heard each other directly. NOTE freq_mhz is stated on BOTH layers of each gateway on purpose: 0 does NOT mean 'back to the node's carrier' -- Node::activate_layer (node.cpp:488) only calls set_rx_freq when freq_mhz > 0, so an inherit-layer entered after an override-layer keeps the PRIOR layer's carrier (a real firmware bug, recorded in BASELINE 26u, NOT fixed here).",
